Title      : PIF: clear the EEPROM right after configuration
Project    : fpga-mister (patch for N64_MiSTer 5725381)
Author     : Konstantin Schmidt (mr_pleasant@gmx.de)
Company    : OHRZ
Created    : 2026-11-05
Description:
  The PIF fills the EEPROM with FF once, on the first second_ena after
  configuration. second_ena counts in VI.vhd and has not run before the game
  starts on the Zybo, so the fill came about a second after the first ROM load,
  when savemem had already loaded the .eep from the card: the game found a blank
  EEPROM, initialized it, and autosave overwrote the file. The fill
  now starts on the first clock after configuration, before Main can load
  anything. The EEPROM holds the same FF when nothing is loaded; the RTC keeps
  using second_ena.
--- a/rtl/PIF.vhd	2026-11-05 09:57:35.851156165 +0100
+++ b/rtl/PIF.vhd	2026-11-05 09:57:35.883958584 +0100
@@ -401,7 +401,7 @@
          cic_input_first <= '0';
          cic_input_ena   <= '0';
          
-         if (second_ena = '1' and INITDONE = '0') then
+         if (INITDONE = '0') then
             INITDONE     <= '1';
             EEPROMState  <= EEPROM_CLEAR;
          end if;
